# Default set vocabulary (a Dewey-like classification for personal archives).
#
# Copied to <home>/sets.rec on first use; edit that copy. Each disc belongs to
# one set. The Code (2-8 capital letters or digits) appears in disc ids
# (PHOTO-07_2015-2024_Q); the Class number gives shelf order and hierarchy:
# hundreds are divisions, tens are sets, units are sub-sets (e.g. 111 TRIP is
# under 110 PHOTO, which is under 100 Memories). Records without a Code are
# division headings. Class numbers, like Dewey's, are never reused for a
# different meaning: add new ones instead.

%rec: Set
%key: Class
%mandatory: Class Name
%type: Class int

Class: 0
Name: General
Description: mixed or unsorted material

Class: 10
Code: MISC
Name: Miscellaneous
Description: material that fits nowhere else yet

Class: 100
Name: Memories
Description: personal photos, video and audio

Class: 110
Code: PHOTO
Name: Photos
Description: photographs from cameras and phones

Class: 111
Code: TRIP
Name: Trips and holidays
Description: photos and video from travel

Class: 112
Code: FAMILY
Name: Family
Description: family life, children, relatives

Class: 113
Code: EVENT
Name: Events
Description: weddings, birthdays, celebrations, gatherings

Class: 120
Code: VIDEO
Name: Home video
Description: video recordings and home movies

Class: 130
Code: AUDIO
Name: Audio recordings
Description: voice memos, recordings, own music

Class: 200
Name: Records
Description: documents and paperwork

Class: 210
Code: SCAN
Name: Scans
Description: scanned paper documents and photos

Class: 211
Code: LETTERS
Name: Letters and correspondence
Description: letters, cards, email printouts

Class: 220
Code: LEGAL
Name: Legal and identity
Description: contracts, certificates, passports, wills, deeds

Class: 230
Code: TAXES
Name: Taxes
Description: tax returns and supporting documents

Class: 231
Code: FINANCE
Name: Finance
Description: bank statements, invoices, insurance, payslips

Class: 240
Code: HEALTH
Name: Health
Description: medical records, prescriptions, test results

Class: 250
Code: HOME
Name: Home and property
Description: house, renovations, manuals, warranties

Class: 300
Name: Work and study

Class: 310
Code: WORK
Name: Work
Description: job and career material

Class: 320
Code: SCHOOL
Name: School and study
Description: courses, notes, theses

Class: 400
Name: Projects
Description: things you made

Class: 410
Code: CODE
Name: Software
Description: source code and programming projects

Class: 420
Code: ELEC
Name: Electronics
Description: circuits, PCBs, firmware, hardware projects

Class: 430
Code: DESIGN
Name: Design and art
Description: drawings, CAD, 3D printing, graphics

Class: 440
Code: WRITING
Name: Writing
Description: articles, stories, blogs, books

Class: 500
Name: Collections
Description: things you gathered rather than made

Class: 510
Code: BOOKS
Name: Books and papers
Description: e-books, articles, reference material

Class: 520
Code: MEDIA
Name: Media library
Description: films, music albums, podcasts

Class: 530
Code: GAMES
Name: Games
Description: games, saves, mods

Class: 600
Name: Backups and exports

Class: 610
Code: BACKUP
Name: System backups
Description: computer backups and disk images

Class: 620
Code: PHONE
Name: Phone backups
Description: phone backups and exports

Class: 630
Code: EMAIL
Name: Email and messages
Description: mailbox exports, chat exports

Class: 640
Code: WEB
Name: Web archives
Description: saved websites (WARC), social media exports
